{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">If a value can be calculated from other state, calculate it every render instead of storing it separately — there's nothing to keep in sync if there's only one copy.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">A useEffect whose only job is setting one state variable from another is a sign the derived value should be a plain expression (or useMemo for performance) instead of its own state.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">State should hold the smallest set of values that can't be derived from anything else — everything else is a view computed on demand, which can't drift by construction.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
